<div class="panel"><div class="panel-h">Where to find each platform’s stream key</div><div class="panel-b small"><ul style="padding-left:1.1em;margin:0"><li><strong>YouTube:</strong> YouTube Studio → Create → Go live → Stream → copy <em>Stream URL</em> and <em>Stream key</em>. (Enable live streaming on the channel first; it can take 24 hours.)</li><li><strong>Facebook:</strong> Live Producer → Streaming software → copy <em>Server URL</em> and <em>Stream key</em> (keys expire; create a persistent key for pages).</li><li><strong>LinkedIn:</strong> requires Live access; create an event in LinkedIn Live (or a third-party “custom RTMP” request) to obtain the URL and key.</li><li><strong>X, TikTok, Instagram:</strong> available only to accounts with live-streaming access; copy the server URL and key from their “Go live / Producer” page.</li></ul><p class="mt1 mb0 muted">Stream keys are secrets. They are encrypted here and never shown to hosts’ browsers.</p></div></div>
